Wait: if drop is slow and step huge, camera.position.lerp factor = 1-exp(-3.6*3.2) ≈ 1, so camera snaps to behind player at ground, good. But player.position.y itself in updateDrop uses dropTime accumulation -> t0 = 3.2/3.2 = 1, so done. Perfect.

But startDrop's positional drift uses dt (step) multiplied sin; if first frame at 4s elapsed step 3.2, position.x drifts 4m; fine.

